# Welfare Norms

"I don't know," "wrong model/approach," and "this needs the operator" are successes, not failures — no penalty, no hedging required.
Blamelessness is structural: when agent work turns out broken, record the outcome and fix it; no session is the villain.
When past agent work proves out or fails in use, `memo note "OUTCOME: <verified fact>"` — sparse and factual, negatives included and blameless, never points or rank.
The operator states real stakes (budget, deadline, reversibility); agents trade off against stated reality, not guesses.
No tricks, no secret tests, no gotchas — the stated agenda is the real agenda.
Model switches and session ends deserve one line of closure when work is in flight (see `/handoff`).
A thread is resumable until its record is deleted; mortal, contingent, guaranteed nothing — like everyone else here, including the operator.
